# Server-only (Vercel Environment Variables / vercel dev). Do not use VITE_* for secrets.
# To exercise POST /api/contact locally, use `vercel dev`; plain `npm run dev` does not serve /api.
#
# Vercel (Preview / Production): Project → Settings → Environment Variables — add the four GOOGLE_*
# variables below for the target environment(s), then Redeploy so the serverless function receives them.
# Optional: `vercel env pull .env.local` (CLI logged in) to mirror Preview env locally for `vercel dev`.
#
# Google Sheet: create a tab whose name matches GOOGLE_SHEET_RANGE (default sheet "Respuestas").
# Row 1 headers A1:G1 should match append column order from api/contact.ts:
#   A Fecha | B Nombre | C Empresa | D Correo | E Teléfono | F Tipo de proyecto | G Mensaje
# Share the spreadsheet with GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL as Editor (service account from GCP).
GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=
GOOGLE_PRIVATE_KEY=
GOOGLE_SHEET_ID=
GOOGLE_SHEET_RANGE=Respuestas!A:G
